PostgreSQL (PostgreSQL License — BSD-style, permissive)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The Memory Context subsystem in src/common/{memcontext,allocset,bump,jm_alloc}.{h,cpp}
is a C++17 port of the algorithm design of:

  - src/backend/utils/mmgr/mcxt.c    (MemoryContext / AllocSet / reset / callback)
  - src/backend/utils/mmgr/aset.c    (power-of-2 freelist, AllocSetAlloc/Free/Reset)
  - src/backend/utils/mmgr/bump.c    (Bump allocator, no per-chunk free)

PostgreSQL is Copyright © 1996–2026, The PostgreSQL Global Development Group.
Licensed under the PostgreSQL License, a BSD-style open source license.
A copy of the PostgreSQL License is available at:
  https://www.postgresql.org/about/licence/

The JiaMiaoDB implementation is an independent C++ rewrite — class names,
APIs, allocator layout, and code structure are original — but the algorithmic
ideas (freelist index, keeper block + dedicated blocks for large allocs,
reset semantics) are derived from the above PostgreSQL source files.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Pugh Skip Lists (academic, no copyright)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The concurrent skip list in src/storage/skiplist.h follows the algorithm of:

  William Pugh, "Skip Lists: A Probabilistic Alternative to Balanced Trees",
  Communications of the ACM, June 1990, 33(6) pp. 668–676.

The single-writer / multi-reader (SWMR) lock-free read path with acquire /
release memory ordering is also inspired by Doug Lea's
java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentSkipListMap (public domain / CC0).

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
zlib CRC32 (public domain)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The CRC32 implementation in src/storage/wal_v3.cpp uses the
Ethernet/zlib polynomial 0xEDB88320. The zlib project is released
into the public domain; see https://www.zlib.net/

